# alias: Mathe
# button-text: Mathe
# scenario-title: --- Mathe over Strong 1!C
# gib-works: false
# bba-works: true
# scenario-title: --- Mathe over Strong 1C
# auction-filter: Auction.....\n1C +
# convention-card-ns: 21GF-DEFAULT
# convention-card-ew: Precision

/*@chat
--- Mathe over Strong 1!C
After East opens an artificial 1!C (Precision, 16+ HCP), South can show:
• X    = both majors, 4-4 or better
• 1NT  = both minors, 4-4 or better
• 1!D, 1!H, 1!S = natural, 5+ cards
Partner (advancer) normally pulls X or 1NT to the better of the advertised
suits; a new suit is natural. Show a 4-4 two-suiter only at favorable
vulnerability -- otherwise be 5-4 or better.
NOTE:  GIB does NOT play this!
https://www.bridgebum.com/mathe_1c.php
@chat*/

# Neither BBA nor GIB plays Mathe.  The filter just keeps East's 1C opening;
# the deals are built so South always has a Mathe call.

dealer east

# East opens strong 1C (Precision): 16+ HCP, any shape
strong1C = hcp(east)>15

# South: enough to act over a strong club, but not a strong hand
sValues = hcp(south)>5 and hcp(south)<14

# South's 4+ card suits
sS4 = spades(south)>3
sH4 = hearts(south)>3
sD4 = diamonds(south)>3
sC4 = clubs(south)>3

# Two-suiters want the values in the two suits
majorHonors = hcp(south,spades)   + hcp(south,hearts) > 3
minorHonors = hcp(south,diamonds) + hcp(south,clubs)  > 3

# South's Mathe calls, in priority order
mX   = sS4 and sH4 and majorHonors                   // X   = both majors
m1N  = sD4 and sC4 and minorHonors and not mX        // 1NT = both minors
m1S  = spades(south)>4   and not (mX or m1N)         // natural spades
m1H  = hearts(south)>4   and not (mX or m1N or m1S)  // natural hearts
m1D  = diamonds(south)>4 and not (mX or m1N or m1S or m1H)  // natural diamonds
mSuit = m1S or m1H or m1D

# Level the three kinds of call so the two-suiters aren't swamped by natural overcalls
HandType_X    = mX
HandType_1N   = m1N
HandType_Suit = mSuit

### BEGIN GENERATED LEVELING ###
noLeveling = 1
levelTheDeal = noLeveling
### END GENERATED LEVELING ###

# Now do it: East opens strong 1C and South has a Mathe call
strong1C and sValues and (mX or m1N or mSuit) and levelTheDeal

action printoneline,

average "X  (majors)  " 100 * mX,
average "1N (minors)  " 100 * m1N,
average "1S natural   " 100 * m1S,
average "1H natural   " 100 * m1H,
average "1D natural   " 100 * m1D,

average "X  is 5-4+   " 100 * (mX  and (spades(south)>4 or hearts(south)>4)),
average "1N is 5-4+   " 100 * (m1N and (diamonds(south)>4 or clubs(south)>4)),

average "hcp South" hcp(south),
average "hcp East " hcp(east),
